// Aiken code - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

# Aiken code is five-bit: digit 1 for a bit 0 and digit 5 for a bit 1, in
# an even number of 1s. Applying it to the ASCII of "Hello World!",
# letter by letter, gives a string of 1s and 5s:
#
# H = 01001000 -> 51515 5 1 5
#
# Aiken was designed for punched cards, where the column is fixed at five
# and a literal 0 or 1 would be confusable with a hole.
